<title>HUNGARY: Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 22.86 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary twelve-month bill yield rises to 22.86 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of twelve-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.86 percent, up from 22.41 percent at an auction two weeks ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said. Full details of the auction follow.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     14,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	 4,846.36 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	     4,846.34 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		  5,500 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.86 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     81.5181 pct</p>
</text>
